WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.192
Constraints are powerful, but timing matters.

00:00:03.192 --> 00:00:11.542
If you add a strict rule before understanding legacy data, valid historical exceptions may be blocked or the

00:00:11.542 --> 00:00:13.382
migration may fail. Profile first.

00:00:13.382 --> 00:00:18.242
Resolve existing violations. Confirm the business rule and its owner.

00:00:18.242 --> 00:00:21.557
Then add the constraint and monitor future data.

00:00:21.557 --> 00:00:27.502
Once a quality rule is well understood, prevention may be better than repeated cleanup.

00:00:27.502 --> 00:00:31.762
Constraints can stop known invalid values at write time.

00:00:31.762 --> 00:00:37.922
When updates are required, preview the target rows, change only what is justified,

00:00:37.922 --> 00:00:42.304
and use RETURNING or an audit log so the transformation can be reviewed.
